  "decision_conditions": [
    "The roof area of the extension hereby permitted shall not be used as a balcony, roof garden or similar amenity area without the grant of further specific permission from the local planning authority.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents: DAAGROUP\nNoise Impact Assessment, Fire Safety Strategy, A.22.025.500, A.22.025.501 A, A_22_025_501B, AC UNIT SPECIFICATIONS TABLE FOR ARXM-R",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town\nand Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (or\nany order revoking and re-enacting that order with or without modification), no\ndevelopment which would otherwise fall within Classes A, AA, B, D, F in Part 1 of\nSchedule 2 to that Order shall be carried out without the prior written\npermission of the local planning authority.",
    "The rating level of the noise emitted from the site shall be at least\n10dB below the existing background noise level. The noise levels shall be\ndetermined at the boundary of the nearest noise sensitive premises. The\nmeasurements and assessment shall be made in accordance to the latest British\nStandard 4142 and BS8233",
    "The window(s) in the flank elevation(s) of the proposed development shall:\n(a) be of purpose-made obscure glass,\n(b) be permanently fixed closed below a height of 1.7m above finished floor level,\nand shall thereafter be retained in that form.",
    "Within 3 months of the date of\nthis decision, a detailed hard and soft landscaping scheme shall be submitted\nto the Local Planning Authority for approval in writing. The scheme shall\nreflect the as-built condition and include proposals for any necessary remedial\nor enhancement works. The scheme must include the following:1.       \nRefuse Storage•         Confirmation that\nrefuse storage is located in the rear garden. Provision must be made for three\nbins, with the store being secure, screened, and visually unobtrusive from the\npublic realm. 2.       \nHard and Soft Landscaping of the Frontage•         A revised layout of\nhard and soft landscaping to the front garden must be submitted. Soft landscape\nworks shall include: planting plans (at a scale not less than 1:100), schedules\nof plants, noting species, plant sizes, plant container sizes (all at time of\nplanting) and proposed numbers / densities. Hard landscape works shall\ninclude; details of boundary treatments (materials, scale of boundary,\nlocation) and  details of hard surfacing materials to be used in the\nlandscaping of the site, Written specification of planting and cultivation\nworks to be undertaken, A landscape implementation programme with proposed\ntiming / dates for the works.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n The development shall be\ncarried out in accordance with the details as so agreed and within 6 months of\nthe date of such approval of details.",
    "Within 3 months of the date of\nthis decision details of shelters, racks, dimensions and location of cycle\nparking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local\nplanning authority. The cycle storage shall be installed within 3 months of the\ndetails as so approved pursuant to this condition and retained thereafter. \n\n\n\nNOTE:  Cycles parking spaces\nshould be secure and sheltered.  LB Harrow do not support the provision of\nvertical cycle storage systems as this excludes less able people from being\nable to securely store their cycle. "
  ],
